The '''Castejón Metro Soportújar Line''' ({{Lang-bl|Linia de Metro de Castejón a Soportújar}}) is a [[W:Rapid transit|subway]] line in [[Castejón]], [[Balisca]], operated by the [[Castejón Metro]]. The line runs between [[Arraso Station|Arraso]] in [[Calañas]] in the east and [[Mezquitilla Station|Mezquitilla]] ([[Llanito]]) in the west. The official name is '''Line 3 Soportújar Line'''.

The line is named after [[Soportújar]] ({{Literal translation|place of the {{W|arcade (architecture)|arcades}}}}), a [[Planned communities in Balisca|new town]] and [[W:Interchange station|interchange station]] that it passes through. On maps and signboards, the line is shown in chartreuse. Stations carry the letter "S" followed by a two-digit number. 

